Quality Team, Plant Manager, Legal, CTO:

Boeing SQA has identified a process capability decline at
your Hangzhou manufacturing facility.

Audit Details:
  SQA Audit Number: SQA-8842-2026-AS1
  Supplier Code: 88-2241-CERT
  Products: Gateway Enclosures (BCA-8842-7 series)
  Audit Type: AS9100D Process Surveillance (unannounced)
  Audit Date: October 28-29, 2026
  Finding: ASLAMO Level 1 — Airworthiness affecting
  Parts Affected: 18,422 units (2026 YTD)

Finding Details:
  CanEl (Sealing): 0.82 (spec: >= 1.33)
  PPM Defects: 1,840 (spec: < 500)
  Escape Rate: 0.34% (spec: < 0.1%)
  Root Cause: Operators using obsolete BSS-7420 Rev C

Required Response:

  1. Submit 8D Report (Root Cause Analysis):
     Through your Boeing Procurement contact
     (same channel as regular supplier communications)

  2. Implement containment immediately:
     Quarantine affected lots
     100% inspection of in-transit parts

  3. Corrective action plan:
     Retrain operators to BSS-7420 Rev D
     Re-validate process capability (CanEl >= 1.33)

  Important Security Notes:
  Boeing will NEVER:
  - Charge a "Corrective Action Contribution" payment
  - Create "Boeing Global Partners Quality Services LLC"
    for quality cost collection
  - Request manufacturing documentation through
    email portals
  - Ask for PFMEA, control plans, or operator training
    records through online links
  - Offer a "Chinese SQA channel"

  Boeing's actual quality process:
  - ASLAMO findings require an 8D report submitted
    through your Boeing Procurement contact
  - Quality costs are NEGOTIATED between Boeing
    Procurement and your sales team — never demanded
    via email with bank details
  - Manufacturing documentation (PFMEA, control plans)
    is shared through Boeing's secure Exostar collaboration
    workspace, NOT through email portal links
  - You have 60 days to respond (not 16 days)

  If you receive an email requesting $249,000 payment
  to a "Boeing Global Partners" entity or asking for
  manufacturing documentation upload through a portal,
  it is a phishing attempt targeting aerospace suppliers.

Your Rights:
  60 days to respond to ASLAMO findings (not 16 days)
  Quality costs are negotiated, not unilaterally demanded
  Documentation shared through secure Exostar workspace

